    // express the full kernel as a single pure Halide Func. Instead, we:
    //
    //   - Keep the outer loops over i and the lower-triangular loop over j
    //     (0 <= j < i) on the host, as required to preserve the sequential
    //     dependencies in the Crout/Doolittle update of L.
    //   - Use a scalar Halide Func to compute each inner summation over k
    //     for the "L" part:
    //       sum_{k<j} A[i][k] * A[k][j]
    //   - Use a *vectorized* Halide Func to compute, in one shot, the entire
    //     "U" part of row i:
    //       for all j in [i, n):
    //           A[i][j] - sum_{k<i} A[i][k] * A[k][j]
